== proof: retention_policies ==
 seq |   table_name    |   keep   |          anchor_label          |  action   |                               why                               
-----+-----------------+----------+--------------------------------+-----------+-----------------------------------------------------------------
   1 | sessions        | 30 days  | after the session started      | delete    | a session that old has expired anyway
   2 | login_events    | 1 year   | after the sign-in              | delete    | long enough to investigate an incident
   3 | support_tickets | 2 years  | after the ticket was closed    | anonymise | anonymised rows still count in support statistics
   4 | consents        | 5 years  | after consent was withdrawn    | delete    | proof of consent and of its withdrawal (art. 7(1))
   5 | dsar_events     | 3 years  | after the request was answered | delete    | accountability (art. 5(2)) for the period complaints are likely
   6 | dsar_requests   | 3 years  | after the request was answered | delete    | accountability (art. 5(2)) for the period complaints are likely
   7 | bank_accounts   | 1 year   | after leaving the scheme       | delete    | time to pay the last refunds
   8 | credentials     | 1 year   | after leaving the scheme       | delete    | a member who left signs in rarely after a year
   9 | beneficiaries   | 10 years | after leaving the scheme       | delete    | as long as benefits can be claimed
  10 | contributions   | 10 years | after leaving the scheme       | delete    | pension and tax records
  11 | legal_holds     | 1 year   | after the hold was released    | delete    | a record that the hold existed
  12 | members         | 10 years | after leaving the scheme       | anonymise | keeps year of birth, area and dates for scheme statistics
(12 rows)

